.TH DISKWATCHER\-FLEET 1 "September 2026" "mu2edaq-diskwatcher 1.3.0" "Mu2e DAQ Utilities"
.SH NAME
diskwatcher\-fleet.sh \- start, stop or check mu2edaq\-diskwatcher on every DAQ node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh
[\fBstart\fR | \fBstop\fR | \fBstatus\fR | \fBlist\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIHOST\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the per-node
.B start\-mu2edaq\-diskwatcher.sh
or
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-diskwatcher.sh
over
.BR ssh (1)
on each DAQ node, several nodes at a time, and prints one line per node and a
summary.
It is meant to be run from
.B mu2e\-mgr\-01
but works from any machine whose ssh reaches the nodes without a prompt.
.PP
The checkout is a shared NFS directory, so the same path is used on every node
(the directory this script lives in, unless
.B \-\-dir
says otherwise) and each node writes its runtime files under its own
.BR run/ \fIhost\fR/
inside it.
.PP
With no
.I HOST
arguments, every node that has a generated file in
.B config/nodes/
is used, plus
.B mu2e\-dl\-01
with its hand-written
.BR config/mu2e\-diskwatcher\-dl\-01.yaml .
A node's config is looked up by name:
.IR config/nodes/mu2e\-diskwatcher\- short .yaml
first, then the same name under
.BR config/ .
A node with no config file is skipped and reported.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B start
The default.
Starts the daemon on each node, replacing any copy already running there, then
fetches
.B /api/health
on the node and reports its status, version, entry count and poll age.
The web server binds only after the first poll completes, so the check allows
up to 30 seconds.
.TP
.B stop
Stops the daemon on each node.
.TP
.B status
Fetches
.B /api/health
on each node without changing anything.
A node that does not answer on the port is reported
.BR DOWN .
.TP
.B list
Prints the node-to-config mapping and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the ssh command for each node; run nothing.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Nodes to work on at once.
Default:
.BR 8 .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Log in as
.I USER
instead of the current user.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Checkout path on the nodes.
Default: this checkout's own path.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR
Domain appended to short names.
Default:
.BR fnal.gov .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Dashboard port, forwarded to the start script as
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
and used by
.BR status .
Default:
.B $CRS_PORT_HTTP
or
.BR 5002 .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
ssh connect timeout.
Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-jump " " \fIHOST\fR
Reach the nodes through
.I HOST
.RB ( "ssh \-J" ),
for running from outside the DAQ network, e.g.
.BR "\-J mu2egateway01.fnal.gov" .
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIHOST\fR
Skip
.IR HOST ;
may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Allow ssh to prompt for passwords or host keys.
By default
.B BatchMode=yes
is set so an unreachable or unauthenticated node fails fast instead of hanging
the batch.
Unknown host keys are still accepted
.RB ( StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new );
a node reported as
.B "UNREACHABLE Host key verification failed"
has a key that
.I changed
since it was last recorded in
.BR ~/.ssh/known_hosts ,
typically after a reinstall, and needs that entry removed.
.PP
When
.B \-\-jump
names a host that is itself in the node list (the gateways are), that node is
reached directly rather than through itself.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
After
.BR start ,
do not fetch
.B /api/health
from each node.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-replace
Forward
.B \-\-no\-replace
to the start script, so a node already running is left alone and reported as
failed rather than restarted.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per node, in node order within each batch:
.PP
.nf
    mu2e-trk-03      OK ok v1.3.0, 8 entries, poll 2.1s ago, up 4s, 0 config issue(s), peers 0/0 ok
    mu2e-calo-07     UNREACHABLE ssh: connect to host ... Connection timed out
    mu2egateway02    FAILED exit 1: error: config file not found: ...
    mu2e-crv-01      DOWN no answer on port 5002 (curl exit 7)
.fi
.PP
followed by
.BR "summary: N ok, N failed/unreachable, N skipped" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every selected node succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, or no nodes selected.
.TP
.B 3
At least one node failed, was unreachable, or (for
.BR status )
was down.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the watcher everywhere from
.BR mu2e\-mgr\-01 :
.PP
.nf
    tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh
.fi
.PP
Check the fleet:
.PP
.nf
    tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh status
.fi
.PP
Restart only the tracker nodes, four at a time:
.PP
.nf
    tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh start \-j 4 mu2e\-trk\-0{1..9} mu2e\-trk\-1{0..4}
.fi
.PP
Stop everything except the data loggers:
.PP
.nf
    tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh stop \-x mu2e\-dl\-01 \-x mu2e\-dl\-02
.fi
.PP
From a laptop outside the DAQ network, as the shift account, through the
gateway, with the checkout at its NFS path:
.PP
.nf
    tools/diskwatcher\-fleet.sh status \-J mu2egateway01.fnal.gov \-u mu2eshift \\
        \-d /home/mu2eshift/mu2edaq\-diskwatcher
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-diskwatcher (1),
.BR make\-node\-configs (1),
.BR ssh (1)
